<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fen River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fen He</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fen River is the second-largest tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and the longest river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, flowing about 700 kilometres south through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiyuan">Taiyuan</a> to join the Yellow River. Its fertile valley in southern Shanxi was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the State of Jin, whose early capitals and cemeteries lie along it, and it has remained the heart of the province.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fen-river.jpg" alt="Fen River" width="320" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Shannon1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yellowrivermap.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
